- Line 67: exact input `{"manuscript":{"p":"[[x]]"}}` with `TOKEN_PATHS["x"]="search.databases[abc].searched_on"` demonstrates that `int(part[1:-1])` raises `ValueError` instead of returning unresolved. Consequence: one bad declared path crashes the audit rather than reporting the token as refusable.

- Line 102: exact input `{"manuscript":{"p":"[[ci-low]]"}}` demonstrates a selector keyed to a form the regex does not use, because `TOKEN` only matches `[a-z0-9_]+`. Consequence: the paragraph is classified as un-tokened and can evade token resolution.

